lease-id\n                                                :dao.lease/holder \"holder-a\"\n                                                :yin.k/epoch epoch\n                                                :yin.k/transaction\n                                                {:yin.k/arbitration arb}}\n                                :yin.k/enrolled #{(:target w)}\n                                :yin.k/prefix p}}})\n              :status :ok}\n             (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e)))]\n    [r @attaches]))\n\n\n(defn- observer\n  \"The composition's handle observer over reflections: the mirror is\n   stepped until the source answers, so one observation is the source's\n   own outcome.\"\n  [peer]\n  (fn [h op arg]\n    (loop [n 6]\n      (s/serve-mirror! peer)\n      (let [r (case op\n                :next (stream/next h arg)\n                :cursor (stream/cursor h arg))]\n        (if (and (= :dao.stream/blocked (:dao.stream/outcome r)) (pos? n))\n          (recur (dec n))\n          r)))))\n\n\n(defn- read-live\n  \"One recorded live read of the lowered tenure `m`: observe, record,\n   settle.  Answers [machine recorded-input].\"\n  [w cp m]\n  (let [stepped (reader/step m (appender w) (observer (:peer cp)))\n        _ (answer! w)\n        drained (reader/drain (:machine stepped) (:replies w))]\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The stage-D gate's compose halves, continued: content-store cuts\n;; around both stored objects of the freeze\n;; =============================================================================\n\n\n(defn- cut-store\n  \"Content store `base` whose `position`-th put suffers a cut: `:before`\n  stores nothing and throws, `:after` stores the bytes and throws\n  anyway.  `fired` (an atom) takes the cut address: the process dies\n  there.\"\n  [base position cut fired]\n  (let [n (atom 0)\n        put! (:put-bytes-fn base)]\n    (assoc base :put-bytes-fn\n 